# The aLLManac — the LATEST channel.  Image pins, nothing else.
# =============================================================================
# The dev playground's pins.  See channels/stable.env for what a channel is.
# The rule for this file: a pin moves here FIRST, gets deployed to a box
# nobody teaches on, gets walked, and only then moves to stable.  What is
# here and not in stable is exactly the upgrade under test — keep the
# comment on each line saying what is being validated and since when.
#
# When this channel breaks, the deliverable is a minimal repro filed
# upstream (danny-avila/LibreChat) and linked from the pin's comment, not
# only our workaround — see the admin guide, "Channels."
#
# Still pinned, not `latest`: a moving tag would make "what broke?"
# unanswerable, and the answer is the whole point of the channel.
# =============================================================================

# Under test since 2026-10-11: 0.8.8, the release (built 2026-10-01).  rc4
# ran here from 2026-09-24 and everything below was walked on it; 0.8.8 is
# what to re-walk — the Agent Management API with M2M auth (the seeder's
# forged JWT should go; #16224), the footer emitted with the HTML shell (the
# CUSTOM_FOOTER wall), OpenID discovery retries and the session-TTL refresh
# (#15983), the interface schema (the lockdown keys), memory as an agent
# capability, the design-system refactor vs. the branding asset mounts.
# NEW in 0.8.8 and not yet looked at: attached code workspaces, subagents,
# programmatic tool calling, agent events.  Our capability lists are explicit
# (librechat.yaml, render.py), so none of those should appear — confirm none
# is switched on somewhere other than `capabilities:`.  Same config version
# as rc4 (1.3.17 upstream; we still write 1.2.8).  grype 2026-10-11: 8
# fixable criticals, 30 high — rc4 on the same day's DB: 8 and 46.
#
# Rc3's partial-index bug (the Mongo block) was fixed in rc4 (#16133) and
# walked on the canary docker host 2026-09-24.  Nothing left for us to file.
#
# The NEW namespace.  The repo moved to LibreChat-AI/LibreChat (2026-09), and
# the old ghcr.io/danny-avila/librechat never got 0.8.8 — rc4 is the last
# tag there.  0.8.8 is at ghcr.io/librechat-ai/librechat and at
# registry.librechat.ai/librechat-ai/librechat, the same digest in both;
# upstream's own compose now names the latter.  ghcr here, like everything
# else we pull.  Stable follows when it moves.
LIBRECHAT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/librechat-ai/librechat:v0.8.8@sha256:5b706bcee1ca154a1e2987303aaeca0eb27f97919cccee4bb604226c2f8abf61
# Found 2026-09-15: rc3 gates agent knowledge uploads on FILE_SEARCH.USE per
# role (0.8.7 did not).  Our lockdown sets interface.fileSearch=false, so
# even ADMIN got 403 on every upload.  Fixed on our side with a dedicated
# seeder role (scripts/seed_agents.py); worth asking upstream whether the
# composer's file-search switch is meant to also govern agent knowledge.
# Everything below matches stable until there is a reason for it not to:
# The 2026-10-01 main-stable build (f69b210), past its 7-day cooldown: 2 fixable
# criticals -> 1 (grype 2026-10-11).  main-stable itself was rebuilt 10-11 and
# waits its week.
LITELLM_IMAGE=ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:main-stable@sha256:f63fb81b831b170ec16851e23c36ac5bf52ef106b271406429524a2ed730bbfd
# 09-24 build: 104 fixable criticals -> 7.  Reads the old schema, auth unchanged,
# and it now scopes reads to the owner — so stable waits until `just evals` here
# shows the guides' knowledge still answers through shared agents.
RAG_API_IMAGE=ghcr.io/danny-avila/librechat-rag-api-dev:latest@sha256:13898be3c4ce9ce60d40606c426929d504fef4d89dfddeac966e12fb740cae5c
ADMIN_PANEL_IMAGE=registry.librechat.ai/clickhouse/librechat-admin-panel:latest@sha256:9a78851f84f448eab780ac658c4d17db51974c240492affc789a72d61e35f678
OPENCODE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/anomalyco/opencode:1.18.2

# ---- The control plane.  Both round-tripped 2026-10-12 on throwaway stacks
# with this repo's own config, old version first, then the new one on the
# same volumes.  Stable is on compose.yml's defaults (2.4.1, 26.1.5).
#
# OpenBao 2.4.1 -> 2.6.3 (built 2026-09-23).  Came up sealed on 2.4.1's raft
# data and opened with the old key; the registrar's AppRole read its course
# path and was refused outside it, the backup role took a snapshot, the audit
# log kept writing.  A snapshot restored into a FRESH 2.6.3 vault sealed it
# and only the original key opened it — the paper sheet's case (just
# dr-sheet).  grype 2026-10-12: 26 fixable criticals -> 3 (Go stdlib, x/net).
OPENBAO_IMAGE=openbao/openbao:2.6.3@sha256:a60afafda36337abe833c4a63894bf1095098f29abea4091e7e555a33dd52889
# Keycloak 26.1.5 -> 26.7.4 (built 2026-09-16).  Migrates the database through
# 26.2 .. 26.7 at first boot, ONE WAY: rolling back is restoring keycloak-db
# from before, not moving this pin back.  After it, on the same realm: the
# realm import skipped (no second realm), realm-lock held (email admin-only),
# the registrar's own calls ran (client, roles, user, role holders, the
# autolink flow's two ALTERNATIVE steps), and a browser-shaped sign-in got an
# id_token with email and groups.  Still warns "Hostname v1 options
# [hostname-port]" — KC_HOSTNAME_PORT in compose; a warning on both versions,
# not a failure.  grype 2026-10-12: 6 fixable criticals -> 3 (bcprov, netty).
KEYCLOAK_IMAGE=quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.7.4@sha256:82a77884f3af238beab1e7afd63b5f530e1b5c0590bd7aa60b40a40463e29b2c

